        "original_id": "d753ca76-e73a-5b7d-b4d8-5916b947e07f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gareth Jones, Dave Gahan, Martin Gore, Andy Fletcher\n- Bands: Depeche Mode, Wire, Erasure, Einstürzende Neubauten\n- Places: Basildon, Essex, London, Paris\n- Albums: Beat Pyramid\n\nFacts:\n- Gareth Jones was born in 1954 and is a British music producer and engineer.\n- Gareth Jones is notable for working with Depeche Mode, Einstürzende Neubauten, Wire, and Erasure.\n- Depeche Mode formed in Basildon, Essex, in 1980 as an English electronic band.\n- Depeche Mode consists of founders Dave Gahan, who is lead vocalist, Martin Gore, who plays guitar, keyboards, and vocals, and Andy Fletcher, who plays keyboards and bass guitar.\n- Beat Pyramid was recorded in London and Paris during 2007.\n- Beat Pyramid was produced by Gareth Jones in London.",
